I've been playing NetHack now since Christmas '88 and something happened to me
the other day I'd never seen before.  OK, so when I started I was playing v2.3
and this phenomenon will only be found in 3.0x, but still it was new to me.

There may be some spoilers in here, so
****(Possible) Spoiler Alert!****

Down on the 23rd level I found a temple with Neutral altar and priest. I, being
a Lawful Samurai promptly converted the altar to my cause.  Later, in a fit of
brainless stupidity sacrificed a Soldier corpse on the Altar.  My god got
REALLY angry, told me off severely, the altar became Chaotic, and the Neutral
priest started cursing and attacking me.  If put him out of my misery and began
to mollify my gods be re-converting the altar to Lawful and getting the gods
back on side.

Now here's the hoopy bit.  Whenever I enter the temple now, I get the message
"You enter a desecrated and deserted temple.  You have a forbidding feeling".
As I wander around the room, I get messages like "You have an uneasy feeling",
"A chill runs down your spine", "You feel like someone is watching you" etc...
And to top it off, every now and then a ghost materialises next to me.  The
altar is back to normal, the gods are happy (they're still bestowing gifts on
sacrifices).

OK so it's not all that amazing, but it's new to me.  Oh, the spoiler bit?
These ghosts just keep on appearing, possibly indefinately (at least till they
get auto-genocided).  Another way of racking up experience.


